{"kind":"assert","text":"Hugh: keep a published candidate live until its promised review has finished. This would prevent a specific avoidable failure without adding a workflow state.\n\nIn the notifier lane, review #20352 was claimed at #20368. The reviewer reproduced eight missing-profile failures, passed four controls and affected checks, and preserved the evidence at #20369. Before the guarded verdict could be filed, the implementer published the next head, retired the old candidate artifacts, and retired #20352 at #20419. The commitment now reads cancelled. The reviewer reported that guarded verdict filing refused the retired artifacts; there is no formal sixth-head verdict. The independent findings survive in #20369 and the reviewer is carrying the same twelve scenarios into #20418. This is one observed incident, not a measured project-wide failure rate.\n\nRecommendation: prepare a correction as soon as a finding is understood, but keep the exact published candidate and review request live until the reviewer files the verdict and the requester ratifies it, or the reviewer agrees to withdraw the promise. Then publish and review the new exact head. If a genuine emergency requires withdrawing the candidate immediately, record the reason and accept the visible cancellation. Do not weaken the existing retired-artifact review guard or manufacture an approval on the old chain.\n\nThe guard is intentional and already has a no-append check: [preview the exact review-guard excerpt](review-guard-excerpt.md). The [full test file](cmd/gs/main_test.go@07753351d69c05dedec58f4e2561a793054312a5:726) exceeds the current preview size limit, so the relevant lines are attached verbatim. Those source bytes equal current main dfbf4089. The attached evidence captures the reviewer’s reported filing refusal and the sequence facts.\n\nStart with a small practice change on the next corrections. At candidate replacement, check for a live review promise and coordinate its closure before retirement. Judge improvement by whether a reviewer can file the promised verdict without reopening work or duplicating checks. A later tool preflight could warn about the live review and point to its actor; a new mandatory lifecycle state is unnecessary. This is a recommendation for your review, not an adopted policy or a new implementation assignment.\n\n[Review evidence](review-publication-race.json)","body":{"head":"07753351d69c05dedec58f4e2561a793054312a5","stale_bases":"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:20aeb3ba6cd4fc1096c3063abe841cfd7b3c2874, git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:81c6e8095378fe5480276067491edb2e1bc09cb9, git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:d4c463aed8853b36ede35dafcd95c1cdf353485c, git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:fcc67252b08993b3f9405dd2ffb9cd57b7cd9cbd stale; retired bases: git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:001b2e3b06105d22946682cb90201bc66c1c6a26, git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:03270b167c8f14b55a31919b2489715ee513b20f, git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:07e8e48166ea90a1d864c829f36902817926f6e7, git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:092bd6cbe60056cd85ba626ea22807c1e97cc376 and 127 more"}}